{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, PCA-2000, single profile → 48.5% acc, 46.4% F1). We have zero information about whether the image modality carries any useful signal for this task, which is the most fundamental design question in a multimodal profiling study. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, ResNet50) is the direct single-modality counterpart to config_001, isolating the effect of switching from RNA to image as the sole input while keeping the profile setting (single) and using a standard, well-established encoder (ResNet50). This tells us the standalone image baseline and lets us compare which modality is stronger. 3) Why it is the best next experiment: With only one data point, the highest-value uncertainty to reduce is whether the image modality is informative at all. If image performance is comparable to or exceeds RNA, it justifies investing remaining budget in multimodal fusion experiments. If image is very weak, it redirects effort toward improving the RNA representation (scvi, scgpt) or multiprofile aggregation. This is the simplest, cleanest single-variable comparison available and avoids conflating modality, fusion, and aggregation effects simultaneously."
}

